 ],
 "notes": "Sheet 0 (Zaha Hadid Architects, Sharjah, 2020s): from the air the building is a family of long, tapering white aluminium-clad 'dunes' lying side by side on a diagonal, sharp at the north-east end and blunter at the south-west, the tallest dune at the crest between two lower; a glazed crack and green terraces between the dunes; curved landscape islands with a dark pond and perimeter paving round it. The entrance is a roof oculus (15 m dome, ventilating) at the blunt end; inside, a triangle-perforated skylit atrium, white ribbon stairs and an auditorium (sheet 1, not modelled). Modelled with tapered prisms: three overlapping dunes of 7, 9 and 14 m, the glazed split, two roof gardens, an entrance dome, the apron and three landscape islands with a pond. Guessed: every dimension (a diagonal of about 130 m and a crest of about 14 m, from the aerial and the 15 m dome), the number of dunes (the aerial shows three or four), the green terraces' positions. Orientation is the aerial's, long axis south-west to north-east. A public corporate building, at its own spot (OpenStreetMap 'BEEAH Group Headquarters', way 1077753326, via Nominatim); the footprint is not yet redrawn from the map's outline."
